  "lifecycle": "Each arm/root pair uses a fresh worker with both model weights and both contexts provisioned. Immediate same-arm warmup followed by resident measurement on those contexts. No context construction, full-KV export/import or numerical reference replay in service. Model/context setup and warmup retained separately.",
  "reference_scope": "Each lane already passed original-R/observer, complete requested-vector and selected committed-state development qualification. New blind roots get independent unchanged original-R free endpoints; every warm/measure endpoint and full producer/pending/termination trace is checked. No full-vector/KV claim is made for clean confirmation slots.",
  "service": "Complete synchronized resident service, including reset, planning, requested output copies, decode and teardown; initial plan clock nested in first warm request. Setup outside service is retained, never free.",
  "primary": "Per-family ratios of total complete measured resident service: LOCAL-D4/SIMPLE-D4 and LOCAL-D4/min(SIMPLE-M,LOCAL-M). Report BOTH fixed M contrasts with multiplicity adjustment; no corrected-min shortcut.",
  "secondary": "Equal-root geometric service ratios; absolute costs, adverse roots, all15 paired contrasts and phase/setup work. Do not pool families or historical samples.",
  "uncertainty": "Fixed10000 root-cluster bootstrap draws per family, PCG64 seed SHA256(seed|bootstrap|family) first8bytes little-endian; linear percentile quantiles. Resample8 roots with all6 repetitions and all6 arms together. Primary3 fixed contrasts use Bonferroni98.333333% percentile intervals per contrast within family; all15 descriptive contrasts use Bonferroni99.666667% intervals. Geometric mean of per-root six-session service-sum ratios remains secondary. Bootstrap intervals with8 roots are approximate, no significance target.",
  "failures": "Retain every failure, partial output and reservation. A blind numerical/lifecycle mismatch closes this version and stops remaining confirmation; no input replacement or timing retries. Engineering repair cannot replace a completed measurement.",
